      "message": "This actually does a deep copy comparison - which means you don\u0027t even have to deal with a set of id separately:\n\n  unique_resources \u003d []\n  for resource in resource_list:\n      if resource not in unique_resources:\n          unique_resources.append(resource)\n  return unique_resources\n\nAnd while this probably isn\u0027t likely in our specific case - it works with the following data set:\n\n  d1 \u003d {\u0027id\u0027: 1, \u0027foo\u0027: \u0027bar\u0027}\n  d2 \u003d {\u0027id\u0027: 1, \u0027foo\u0027: \u0027baz\u0027}\n\nWhere-as only comparing ID and assuming both dictionaries are equal based on the id only means ^ those are equal.",
